-- title:
--   Coordinate Brownian Motion for the Joint Natural Filtration
-- statement:
--   This states that every coordinate of a multidimensional Brownian motion remains Brownian relative to the joint natural filtration.
--
--   Let $(\Omega,\mathcal F,P)$ be a probability space, let $d\in\mathbb N$, let $W$ be a `MultidimBrownianMotion` with $d$ coordinates, and let $j\in\operatorname{Fin}(d)$. Write $W^j$ for the $j$-th coordinate and let $\mathcal F^W$ be the joint natural filtration generated by all coordinates. Then
--
--   $$\operatorname{IsBrownianFiltration}(W^j,\mathcal F^W).$$
--
--   Thus the coordinate process has the Brownian-filtration properties with respect to the larger filtration generated by the complete vector-valued process. This is a technical compatibility result for multidimensional constructions.
--
